    <h2>What local SEO is — and isn't</h2>
    <p>For a Kalispell service business, "SEO" is mostly three things: a complete, active Google Business Profile; a fast site that says clearly what you do and where; and steady reviews. That's it. Nobody can promise you a ranking, and anyone who does is selling you a report.</p>
    <div class="proof-points">
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>The map pack comes first</strong>
        <span>Search "near me" for almost any local service and the map with three businesses sits above every website. Your Google profile decides whether you're in it.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>An active listing gets found</strong>
        <span>Calls, bookings and reviews through your listing tell Google you're real and open for business. That's why we build the front desk and the search work as one system. <a href="/post/how-local-customers-find-you/">Read how it connects &rarr;</a></span>
      </div>
      <div class="ppoint">
        <strong>Fewer, better pages beat a page farm</strong>
        <span>One honest page per service and one for your town outrank a hundred copy-pasted "city pages." We won't build you those.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
